## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical multi-tenant isolation, policy-as-code, and operational testing in GCP.

## Key Concepts

- Shared VPC and host projects
- IAM Conditions for per-tenant access
- VPC Service Controls for data exfil prevention
- Billing Budgets and cost monitoring per tenant
- Cloud Asset Inventory for drift detection
- CI/CD with Terraform and Cloud Build
- Policy-as-code (OPA) and guardrails

## Code Example

```javascript
// sample budget per tenant
resource "google_billing_budget" "tenant_budget" {
  billing_account = var.billing_account_id
  display_name    = "tenant-${var.tenant_id}-budget"

  amount {
    specified_amount {
      currency_code = "USD"
      units         = 1000
    }
  }

  threshold_rules {
    threshold_percent = 0.8
    spend_basis       = "CURRENT_SPEND"
  }

  // optional fields omitted for brevity
}
```

```javascript
// per-tenant IAM condition (example)
resource "google_project_iam_member" "tenant_view" {
  project = var.tenant_project_id
  role    = "roles/viewer"
  member  = "user:${var.user_email}"
  condition {
    title       = "tenant_is_owner"
    expression  = "resource.name.startsWith('projects/${var.tenant_project_id}')"
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test drift between intended IAM bindings and actual bindings?  
- How would you handle onboarding/offboarding tenants without disruptive outages?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses real-world skills in GitOps, policy-as-code, cross-region DR, and automated rollback.

## Key Concepts
- GitOps and Cloud Deploy
- Policy-as-code with OPA
- CMEK and IAM Conditions
- Canary traffic routing across GKE/Cloud Run
- Drift detection and regional failover

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: trigger a rollback if a metric breaches a threshold
async function maybeRollback(metrics) {
  if (metrics.latency > 500 || metrics.errorRate > 0.02) {
    await cloudDeploy.rollback();
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test drift detection across regions?
- How do you simulate regional outages and verify failover?

Why This Is Asked: Tests ability to design progressive delivery with multi-region, no manual hacks. Key Concepts: Cloud Deploy pipelines, region-scoped traffic controls, Cloud Run traffic splits, Cloud Monitoring alerting, automatic rollback, minimal IAM. Code Example:```javascript
const deployConfig = {
  pipeline: 'region-canary',
  stages: [
    { region: 'us-east1', canary: 0.05, durationMin: 20 },
    { region: 'global', canary: 0.20, durationMin: 30, guard: 'latency<0.85' }
  ],
  rollback: 'setTraffic(v3)';
};
```
